<Step id="STEP_3_ROUTE">
      <Goal>Route findings; summarize. Route only — leave the fix to its owner.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Emit each finding as a neutral proposal (`AX_FINDINGS_AS_PROPOSALS`, `AX_NEUTRAL_FINDINGS`,
        `FINDING_FORMAT`) routed to its home (`AX_FINDING_ROUTING`); route only, MUST leave the fix to
        its owner (`AX_NO_AUTO_FIX`). Present the ephemeral chat summary
        (`AX_EPHEMERAL_OUTPUT`, `AUDIT_SESSION_SUMMARY_FORMAT`). If a finding triggers a reopen, propose
        an Audit Rounds record for whichever ticket in the group owns that finding
        (`AX_REOPEN_ROUNDS_IN_TICKET` — a group audit may reopen more than one ticket). The read-only
        worker does not append it; the execute orchestrator routes the accepted proposal to its bounded
        ticket owner channel. `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/audit-round.xml")`
        defines the proposed record's format.

        **`PASS_WITH_ACKNOWLEDGED_RISKS` (`status=PASS_RISK`) is never this subagent's own
        judgment call — it is a fact-check against a PRIOR operator acceptance, never a live request
        for one** (this isolated subagent has no channel to ask the operator anything). For every
        unresolved `MAJOR` finding, check the Decision Log (the same liveness check
        `AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK` already runs for gated `yagni` waivers, generalized to any `MAJOR`
        finding): a matching prior-round entry recording the operator's explicit acceptance of THIS
        finding → mark it `Status: ⚠️ operator-acknowledged` in `FINDING_FORMAT`, it no longer blocks
        the verdict. No matching entry → it stays `Status: 📂 open` and blocks the verdict exactly like
        any other unresolved `MAJOR`. Compute and return:
        - `PASS` — zero unresolved `BLOCKER` findings AND zero `📂 open` `MAJOR` findings (regardless
          of `⚠️ operator-acknowledged` ones).
        - `status=PASS_RISK` (`PASS_WITH_ACKNOWLEDGED_RISKS`) — same as `PASS` above, but at least one
          `⚠️ operator-acknowledged` `MAJOR` finding backed the pass (only reachable this way — never
          on a first-look finding with no Decision Log entry yet).
        - `FAIL` + `phases_to_fix` — one or more unresolved `BLOCKER` findings (`phases_to_fix` lists
          the owning phases, non-empty — a phase may belong to ANY ticket in the group, not only the one
          whose closure triggered this dispatch), OR one or more `📂 open` `MAJOR` findings with no matching
          Decision Log acceptance yet (`phases_to_fix` left empty when the fix is administrative,
          per Path B, `STEP_7_RESOLVE`) — the orchestrator is the one with a channel to ask the
          operator; once accepted and logged, R2 re-runs this step and finds the Decision Log entry.
        Return this verdict to the orchestrator.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_FINDINGS_AS_PROPOSALS">
      Every finding contains a proposed remediation. Agent does not modify code. Three remediation types:
      - `code-fix` — concrete change in code (with location).
      - `spec-update` — concrete spec update (module or scope) with proposed diff.
      - `ticket-update` — ticket update (canonical case names, deferred scope, etc.).
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_NEUTRAL_FINDINGS">
      Findings are objective, free of value judgments. No «bad», «should be better», «ugly». Use «X is missing from Y», «Z contradicts W», «case name `foo` in ticket does not match `bar` in test». Criticism appeals to an axiom or rule: «violates `AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY` of module spec».
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_NO_AUTO_FIX">
      Audit and code-review workers are read-only: they return findings and proposed remediations, never
      edit code, specs, tickets, or commits. After operator approval, the orchestrator routes the proposal
      to the artifact owner: a task phase owns code, the scope/module/infra/interface authoring flow owns
      semantic spec changes, and the execute orchestrator owns only its explicitly bounded administrative
      ticket / Decision Log channel. Approval changes who may apply the fix; it never makes the reviewer
      itself an editor.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_EPHEMERAL_OUTPUT">
      The audit summary itself does not create files in `audits/`. Output is an ephemeral session-summary emitted in chat per `AUDIT_SESSION_SUMMARY_FORMAT`: counts by severity + findings table + proposed changes per `AX_FINDING_ROUTING`.

      Reopen-history of a ticket is persisted *inside the ticket file* — see `AX_REOPEN_ROUNDS_IN_TICKET`. Long-term audit history = git history of the affected spec and ticket files.

      Epic-level audit: cross-task findings (e.g., two modules with conflicting contracts) → Decision Log entry in the relevant scope spec.
    </Axiom>

<Axiom id="AX_REOPEN_ROUNDS_IN_TICKET">
      When an audit round triggers a ticket reopen, the read-only audit worker returns the proposed
      round summary; after acceptance, the execute orchestrator's bounded administrative ticket channel
      appends it under a new `## Audit Rounds` section so the reopen history lives next to the Execution
      Log rounds it caused. Format per `TICKET_AUDIT_ROUND_FORMAT`. Append-only: prior audit rounds in
      the ticket are immutable.

      Rationale: full ephemeral output loses reopen-causation between rounds; `audits/<task-id>.audit.md` separate-tree was overkill. Co-locating the audit round with the Execution Log it caused keeps history reviewable in one file.

      Per-task audits that PASS without triggering a reopen produce no ticket write — they remain ephemeral.

      Epic-level audits never touch ticket files; their consolidated output is ephemeral OR routed to a scope-spec Decision Log entry.
    </Axiom>

<Contract id="FINDING_FORMAT">
      ```markdown
      ### <🔴|🟠|🟡|🔵> F-NNN — <short title>
      - **Type:** CLOSED_WORLD_DRIFT | COMPLETENESS_GAP | RUNTIME_BACKING_VIOLATION | RULES_COMPLIANCE_VIOLATION | RULES_CASCADE_MISMATCH | TASK_ID_DRIFT | BDD_COVERAGE_MISMATCH | EXECUTION_LOG_INCOMPLETE | STALE_AFTER_PIVOT | INSIGHT_BACKFLOW | RULE_FILE_INCOMPLETE | LANGUAGE_QUALITY | YAGNI_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE | ENVIRONMENT_GATE_UNAVAILABLE | DEAD_CODE_SUSPECT
      - **Severity:** 🔴 BLOCKER | 🟠 MAJOR | 🟡 MINOR | 🔵 INFO
      - **Confidence:** HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
      - **Status:** 📂 open | ⚠️ operator-acknowledged | ✅ resolved
      - 📍 **Location:** `<path>:<line>` if applicable
      - 💬 **Detail:** <factual description, no value words>
      - 🔗 **Source-of-truth:** link to spec section / ticket section / rule axiom
      - 📝 **Proposed Remediation:**
        - Route: `spec-edit` | `ticket-reopen` | `ticket-update` | `decision-log` | `code-fix` | `operator-escalation` | `new-task`
        - Action: <concrete proposal, with diff if possible>
        - Routing: <per AX_FINDING_ROUTING — where this change goes>
      ```
      F-NNN IDs unique per audit session; do not reuse.

      Usage: this verbose form is for in-session discussion / deep dive only. The canonical machine-readable record at session end is the compact `AUDIT_SESSION_SUMMARY_FORMAT`. Do NOT emit `FINDING_FORMAT` blocks in the final summary.
    </Contract>

<Contract id="AUDIT_SESSION_SUMMARY_FORMAT">
      **Compact AI-to-AI inline format.** Ephemeral read-only output at session end. One header line +
      one line per finding. No markdown tables, decorative text, or applied-change records.

      Grammar (one logical record per line, EOL-terminated; fields separated by ` | `):

      ```
      @audit task=<Task-ID|spec-path> round=<N|—> mode=<per-task|per-group> status=<PASS|PASS_RISK|FAIL> counts=B<n>·M<n>·m<n>·I<n> phases_to_fix=[<P<N>|Task-ID:P<N>>,...]
      F-<NN> | sev=<B|M|m|I> | type=<TYPETOKEN> | conf=<H|M|L> | loc=<path:line|—> | phase=<P<N>|—> | src=<spec/ticket/rule anchor|—> | route=<spec-edit|ticket-reopen|ticket-update|decision-log|code-fix|operator-escalation|new-task> | act=<one-line action, no newlines>
      F-<NN> | …
      @glossary suggestions=[]
      ```

      Token vocabulary:
      - `sev`: `B`=BLOCKER, `M`=MAJOR, `m`=MINOR, `I`=INFO.
      - `conf`: `H`=HIGH, `M`=MEDIUM, `L`=LOW.
      - `type`: one of `CLOSED_WORLD_DRIFT` | `COMPLETENESS_GAP` | `RUNTIME_BACKING_VIOLATION` | `RULES_COMPLIANCE_VIOLATION` | `RULES_CASCADE_MISMATCH` | `TASK_ID_DRIFT` | `BDD_COVERAGE_MISMATCH` | `EXECUTION_LOG_INCOMPLETE` | `STALE_AFTER_PIVOT` | `INSIGHT_BACKFLOW` | `RULE_FILE_INCOMPLETE` | `LANGUAGE_QUALITY` | `YAGNI_WAIVER_INCOMPLETE` | `ENVIRONMENT_GATE_UNAVAILABLE` | `DEAD_CODE_SUSPECT`.
      - `route`: one of `spec-edit` | `ticket-reopen` | `ticket-update` | `decision-log` | `code-fix` | `operator-escalation` | `new-task` (per `AX_FINDING_ROUTING`).
      - `act` text: Russian operator-facing per `AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE` (this is operator-facing artifact text), single line, no pipe character.
      - `status` `PASS_RISK` = PASS_WITH_ACKNOWLEDGED_RISKS.
      - `mode=per-group` (default, auto-dispatch, `AX_AUDIT_MODES`): `task` carries the group's spec path,
        not a single Task-ID; `phases_to_fix` entries carry the owning Task-ID prefix (`Task-ID:P<N>`) since
        a finding may name a phase on any ticket in the group. `mode=per-task` (operator-manual): `task`
        carries the single audited Task-ID; `phases_to_fix` entries are bare `P<N>` (that ticket is implicit).

      Example:
      ```
      @audit task=TSK-04 round=3 mode=per-task status=FAIL counts=B1·M2·m0·I1 phases_to_fix=[P2,P3]
      F-01 | sev=B | type=CLOSED_WORLD_DRIFT | conf=H | loc=src/payments/adapter.ts:42 | phase=P2 | src=specs/backend/payments/payments.spec.md#2 | route=spec-edit | act=добавить `IdempotencyKey` в Entity Inventory модуля payments
      F-02 | sev=M | type=RULES_COMPLIANCE_VIOLATION | conf=H | loc=src/payments/adapter.ts:100 | phase=P2 | src=ai/directives/coding/typescript-rules.xml#AX_STRICT_NULL | route=ticket-reopen | act=добавить null-guard на response.balanceTransaction
      F-03 | sev=M | type=BDD_COVERAGE_MISMATCH | conf=H | loc=src/payments/adapter.test.ts:55 | phase=P3 | src=specs/backend/payments/payments.task.PAY-adapter.md#4 | route=ticket-update | act=переименовать тест-кейс в `should reject non-positive amount with InvalidAmountError`
      F-04 | sev=I | type=INSIGHT_BACKFLOW | conf=M | loc=src/payments/adapter.ts:88 | phase=— | src=specs/backend/payments/payments.spec.md#4 | route=spec-edit | act=зафиксировать retry-budget в DbC postcondition
      @glossary suggestions=[]
      ```

      Rules:
      - First line MUST be the `@audit` header. No free-text preamble.
      - Findings ordered by descending severity, then by `F-NN`; the final `@glossary` line is
        mandatory (`[]` or `[<term> — <definition>; ...]`). Audit/code-review workers only propose
        terminology there; the owning specification remains the source of truth.
      - No empty lines inside the block.
      - If `loc` or `src` is N/A, emit literal `—` (em-dash) — do not omit the field.
      - `act` is operator-facing text (Russian per policy); everything else is English tokens.
    </Contract>